WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.590
ano toki umareta no

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.590
あのとき生まれたの

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.590
I'll softly give you my thoughts

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.120
watashi no omoi sotto ageru

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.120
私の想いそっとあげる

00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:09.120
That were born at that moment

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.010
shinjite ite

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.010
信じていて

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.010
Please believe in them

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.450
deatta hi kara

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.450
出逢った日から

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:28.450
Since the day when we met

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.710
hajimete no kimochi megutteru

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.710
初めての気持ち巡ってる

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.710
For the first time, I have these feelings, and they go around

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.740
honto no egao hoshii nante

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.740
ホントの笑顔ほしいなんて

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.740
I want your true smile

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.620
anata ga oshiete kureta sorao

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.620
あなたが教えてくれた空を

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:42.620
I embrace the sky

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.740
dakishimete yume o miru

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.740
抱きしめて夢をみる

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:47.740
That you told me about and dream

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.590
tooi keredo・・・

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.590
遠いけれど・・・

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.590
It's faraway, but...

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.800
atatakai hikari no kakera

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.800
あたたかい光のかけら

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:54.800
The fragments of warm light

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.600
kizutsuita hane ni inochi o kureta no

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.600
傷ついた羽根に命をくれたの

00:00:54.970 --> 00:01:00.600
Gave life to my wounded wings

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.010
fureta toki umareta

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.010
触れたとき生まれた

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.010
Born at the moment when we touched

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.090
tsuyoi watashi no soba ni

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.090
強い私のそばに

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.090
Next to me, who is strong

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.290
mamoraretai watashi ga nemutte ita no

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.290
守られたいわたしが眠っていたの

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:13.290
The me who wants to be protected was asleep

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.310
sou unmei kaerareru ne

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.310
そう運命変えられるね

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.310
That's right, destiny can be changed

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:26.370
futari no koi mezamesasete・・・

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:26.370
ふたりの恋目覚めさせて・・・

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:26.370
Let our love awaken...

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:29.940
{last frame of OP}

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.040
See? It's the same as ever, isn't it?

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.620
The repairs haven't been completed yet.

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.000
They really aren't very responsible.

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.210
Don't you think so, Murasaki?

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.990
I do not know.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:49.910
Father is hopeless.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:51.550
He is too careless with everything.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:55.500
I almost lost my precious little sister.

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.470
There isn't even someone to replace you.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.390
Is that so?

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:13.490
Murasaki.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:15.610
Don't step on the threshold.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.960
Do you want to step on father's head?

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.960
Note: A saying to scare children, but actually used to teach manners.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.330
Not a bad joke at all.

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:28.870
Tenth Episode 「Accustomed Fear」

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.840
What are you doing?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.600
I'm asking you what you are doing.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.840
I spilled my tea.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.100
I did it, so I should take care of it.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:50.320
That is why we have servants.

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.980
I can't do it myself?

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.270
No.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.520
I don't know what you've seen outside,

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.460
but please be obedient.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.930
Tea has been spilt!

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:04.780
Go wipe the table.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.210
Hey, wipe it yourself.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.280
Why? It's your job, isn't it?

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.710
You spilled it, so you have to wipe it up.

00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:19.820
Hey, it'll spill onto the tatami!

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:26.230
I can't even do things myself anymore.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:30.310
When will you put Murasaki back into the Inner Sanctuary?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.670
On the first day of spring, I will...

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:34.660
You intend to let the year pass by?

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.460
Her experiences outside have strongly affected her thoughts and...

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.410
Make her forget them.

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:44.370
Those kinds of feelings are unnecessary for a woman of the Inner Sanctuary.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.160
Yes.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.670
Renjou, do not forget your predecessor's final will.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:51.040
I know.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.170
I could let Ryuuji handle it.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:56.650
No, I will handle it.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:58.010
She is my daughter after all.

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.680
"My daughter," huh?

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:02.410
Yes.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:04.940
I cannot even allow you to let the winter solstice pass.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:07.590
She should be placed in the Inner Sanctuary immediately.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:15.360
Even in this cold weather he mentions the final will, huh?

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.510
It's cold! It's too cold!

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.220
What about the stove?

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.000
In the closet.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.920
You don't have to be so stingy over your electricity bill.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.960
You don't even turn on the lights during the day on weekdays, anyway.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:33.510
You didn't need to say it.

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:35.380
I'm just telling him the truth.

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.970
I'm not talking about that.

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.600
How many days do you think have passed since then?

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.250
How long do you intend to be irresolute?

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:44.370
Recently, those kind of men are okay, you know!

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:46.370
No, they're not.

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:49.510
I'm going shopping.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:52.620
Meat! Meat! Meat!

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.520
Is pork okay?

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.320
Beef, beef!

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.320
Very well, I will treat you all to dinner today. {VLCs for losers. Treat yourself to MPC or something.}

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:04.050
I got some money last night after doing a palm reading for a drunken salaryman.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.180
You worked?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.080
He looked like a man with money, you see.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.810
I told him things that'd make him happy and he coughed up the money just like that.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.620
Isn't that swindling?

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:15.540
We can buy anything!

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.220
I want to try and eat that oyster thing.

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.470
You've never had it before?

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:22.450
Oysters, you see,

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:25.180
are a forbidden food laced with the devil's flavor.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.230
Is that why it has such a disgusting shape?

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:30.360
People become adults if they are able to overcome that, you see.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.130
All right! Let's have oyster soup!

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.060
I'll go!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.820
Very well, I will give you the sword of bravery, boy!

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:42.120
I'll be going now.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.760
Wasn't that trick a bit old?

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.650
The one on top was real, though.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:49.340
Hey.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.640
What?

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:54.170
You were in my room all of last night, right?

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:56.290
Are you sure it wasn't the night before?

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:04.290
We're eating that again?

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.770
We always eat this, though.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.390
Is there something else you want to eat?

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.120
I want the dish called simmered mackerel with miso.

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:18.620
You sure you want that? {check for consistency with what we had in episode whatever}

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.000
What is it?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.580
The shrimp over there is cheaper and tastes better.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:24.900
Really?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.190
Oysters?

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.440
Have you ever eaten it before?

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.350
I have.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.380
It was a fried-oyster lunch box, though.

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:32.900
Do you have a problem with that?

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.250
Not at all.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:42.980
Did you want something?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:44.550
I'm just watching you.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:45.380
Why?

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.590
It'll be troubling if you do something reckless.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.270
Me?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:54.980
Once more.

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:00.810
Thank you.

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.210
That's enough.

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.390
Okay.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.650
Is that the Houzuki-ryuu?

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.950
It's a fighting style that doesn't really have a stance.

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.330
I see.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.260
It'll be a formidable art with more training, though.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:17.790
Once my body is back to normal, I'll be training again.

00:07:17.790 --> 00:07:19.590
That'd be for the best.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:23.200
With the way you are now, it'll be impossible to face someone like the Kuhouins.

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:23.710
You'd die.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.880
I know.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.740
The pain was so bad that I almost couldn't sleep for several days.

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.310
Me too.

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:34.230
I don't ever want to get near that family again.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:37.220
I'm amazed we were even able to take her away.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.850
I get the chills just by remembering it.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:42.770
The Inner Sanctuary was an abnormal place.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.770
It's isolated from the world,

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:50.570
and it felt like whatever happened outside had absolutely nothing to do with it.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:55.840
I knew right away that the child sitting at the back was Murasaki-san.

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:58.230
Her eyes looked dead.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:04.610
She was living locked inside that monstrous house, unable to rely on or talk to anyone.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:09.670
And then you came to my place after that.

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:11.940
I was against it though.

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:16.100
I didn't think you could do it,

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.770
and thought that it was my job.

00:08:18.770 --> 00:08:21.340
And moreover, I failed.

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:24.260
But, it was impossible for me too

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:28.110
Plus, thinking of her daily life,

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.880
I'm sure she had more fun being with you.

00:08:31.880 --> 00:08:34.950
But I was at school during the day,

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.360
so she was mostly with Tamaki-san and Yamie-san.

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.250
I'm just...

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.560
That's not true.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:44.540
I'm sure she's more thankful to you than anyone else.

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:47.000
I couldn't protect her, though.

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:51.280
There are times when things don't go well, too.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.930
I've failed many times also.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:55.220
<i>You </i>did?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:55.970
Of course.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:59.900
I don't even know how many times Benika-san saved me.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:01.230
Really?

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:05.030
There are even people who died because of me.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.270
I was careless...

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:10.400
It was a simple bodyguarding job, too.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.990
Maybe something carbonated is better.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.520
What about your blood sugar levels?

00:09:17.520 --> 00:09:19.010
Please.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:20.870
I want to drink sweet stuff sometimes.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:24.160
I won't be responsible then.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.900
Maybe orange would be better?

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:28.960
Which one, then?

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.680
Orange.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:32.260
I want orange.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.060
It happened in an instant.

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:44.000
I thought it was over for me.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.910
What did Benika-san do after that?

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.560
She told me not to make the same mistake again,

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:00.450
and gave me my next job.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:02.460
The next one...

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:07.830
You may have failed, but Murasaki-san didn't die.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.720
You're better off than me.

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:12.220
Once she enters the Inner Sanctuary, it'll be the same as if she had died.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.210
But she's alive.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.370
She just has nothing to do with us anymore.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:20.630
We have to switch our minds to a new job.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:22.560
I'm not that strong yet.

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.020
No one is that strong.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.520
You become strong when you try to be.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:29.890
Right...

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:32.640
The Kuhouin matter is over.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.200
That name has nothing to do with us anymore.

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.950
I know.

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:40.770
I know, but...

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:43.020
But...

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:48.070
You have to accept it even if it means you have to force yourself to.

00:10:48.070 --> 00:10:49.840
You won't be able to move forward if you don't.

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:52.540
Are you telling me to forget all that has happened?

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:53.890
You're a pro, aren't you?

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.770
Yes...

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:00.890
Morning.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:02.880
Yeah, morning.

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.150
It's unusual for you to be late.

00:11:04.150 --> 00:11:04.980
Really?

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:06.840
Did you get paid or something?

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:07.630
Why?

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:09.130
Because you're in a good mood.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.180
Really?

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:15.360
You're in a good mood when either Juuzawa Benika 
compliments you or you get paid, right?

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:17.660
It's neither.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:19.230
I haven't been working recently.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.130
What about the bodyguarding job?

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:24.390
I failed that one.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.400
I've got nothing to do with that job now.

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:28.830
Anyway, I have to make sure I don't mess up on new jobs.

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:32.880
What?

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:36.460
So you've become a person who can say that.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.800
What do you mean?

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.390
Whatever, that kind of thinking is necessary.

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:43.680
What are you trying to say?

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:45.820
Do you like your current self?

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.600
Don't say something Benika-san would.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:52.320
I was just wondering if you were that honest.

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:53.570
What?

00:11:53.570 --> 00:11:56.470
You even told me that the Kuhouins were a big job and to stay out of it.

00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:59.100
I didn't say it was bad or anything.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.670
I'm sure you're glad you were able to change your mind so easily.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:04.030
Don't say it like that.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:07.960
Next time I'll take on jobs that fit me and do them well.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.890
Maybe, that might suit you the most.

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:16.100
I'm trying to do what you've been telling me to do all this time, so what are you getting at?

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:18.260
I hope it all goes well for you.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.440
Are your injuries okay now?

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:29.190
Yeah, they are.

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:33.150
It's all right, I didn't use this.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:38.360
In the end, I couldn't protect Murasaki,

00:12:38.360 --> 00:12:40.670
I'm still too weak and inexperienced.

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.110
That's not true.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:44.640
It's okay, I lost.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.660
This is my strength right now.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.540
Have you given up?

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.870
I mean, I understand that this is my current strength.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.250
Are you okay with that?

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.740
It's not about that, it just can't be helped.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.580
I've only just begun with this career,

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:00.220
so these things happen.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.050
If there's anything you need help with, please tell me.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.680
I said I'm all right.

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:12.550
Hello?

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:13.680
Ah, what's up?

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:16.690
Hey, what do you normally do when you get home from school?

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.500
Huh? What are you saying?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.360
Is it Shinkurou?

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.620
Well, uh, I was just wondering about what I usually do.

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:23.950
How would I know?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:24.970
Call him over.

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:25.780
You can play games.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.410
Games? I've never played them before, so teach me how.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:30.460
Come over, Shinkurou.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:32.070
Eh? Can I?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.450
Hold on!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:34.060
Do you want me to cut the link?

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:36.210
Hello?

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:36.210
Forget it, let's keep going.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.710
Call me back later, Shinkurou.

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.010
Games, huh?

00:13:43.750 --> 00:13:46.600
I want a game, Shinkurou!

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:52.020
I guess I'll clean.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:58.230
It sure gets clean.

00:14:02.050 --> 00:14:06.740
I'm sure more would come off if I used a cleaner.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.030
Coming!

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:11.880
Um...

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.640
I don't believe I need to move.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.870
This place is too far away for your next job.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:21.880
It'll be the opposite direction when you come home from school.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.370
I've had jobs like that before, though.

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:26.620
It may be a long job.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.690
Do I have to protect someone?

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:30.880
I'll contact you later with the details.

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:32.520
Anyway, just prepare to move for now.

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.090
I see.

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:36.230
Is there anything you need?

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:39.000
No, nothing.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.150
I see.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:46.280
Eh? Why?

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.650
I'm moving.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:51.600
Because of my job.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:54.780
I thought it stank of cigarettes. So, that woman came, huh?

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:56.710
So, you're going to leave?

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.650
Well, yeah.

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:00.910
What an adult thing to do.

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:01.960
What do you mean?

00:15:02.320 --> 00:15:04.630
You really just want to forget your memories, right?

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:06.130
No...

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:08.640
It's because you're always so hesitant!

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.000
I'm not being hesitant or anything.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.180
This is just for my job.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.640
I can't just ignore Benika-san's orders.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.440
Even so, you're acting too cold.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:19.530
What do you mean, "just your job?"

00:15:19.530 --> 00:15:21.880
I'm still a paid pro, though.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:24.770
A pro that can't even protect a 7 year old, huh?

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:25.920
I won't make a mistake next time.

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:28.930
So you're just going to treat Murasaki-chan as a mistake.

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:30.440
What else can I do?

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.790
That's right, they were too strong, right?

00:15:33.790 --> 00:15:34.950
Do you think running away is winning?

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:36.640
Leave me alone!

00:15:37.200 --> 00:15:38.550
I'll be moving out soon.

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:40.010
So you're even running away from this room.

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:41.720
That's enough.

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:44.550
The boy can do what he wants.

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:46.240
All right.

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:51.010
It looks as if we'll get in the way of Shinkurou-kun's growth if we're around. {}

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:58.980
I'm surprised she was able to watch this happily.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:11.990
This was also something Tamaki brought for Murasaki.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.500
It really is different when we have a stove.

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.190
It's like the room has instantly become luxurious.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.000
Now it won't be cold!

00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:29.610
She was so excited over such a simple stove,

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.220
and so happy with a simple futon.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.720
If I didn't come home quickly from school, she'd get angry.

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:37.630
You're late, Shinkurou!

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.580
I'm so hungry I can't stand it anymore!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.090
I was busy.

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.480
There are many things I have to do.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.990
You always, always, say that you're busy.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:50.470
That's right.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:52.280
Because I <i>am </i>busy.

00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:53.740
It's my job.

00:16:55.190 --> 00:16:56.750
It's my job...

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.460
I'm a pro.

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:02.250
Will you swear to protect me?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.630
Do you know what you're saying?

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:14.110
I see.

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:18.060
Shall we meet, then?

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:21.280
It's impossible, you won't just be getting experience out of it.

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:22.390
I'll do it even if it's impossible.

00:17:22.920 --> 00:17:28.680
My promise with Murasaki's mother was only to take her outside and to teach her love,

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.060
and that's been done.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:30.940
What do you mean "love?"

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:37.000
Her mother, Souju, prayed that her daughter could fall in love.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:37.830
With someone from the outside, that is.

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:39.750
Then our job isn't over yet.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:42.480
She wanted her to fall in love, but she's only seven.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.310
It's difficult.

00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:48.130
But I'm sure that Murasaki had feelings of love for you.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.160
I don't think it was feelings of love or anything like that.

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:52.140
She believed in you, though.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:53.370
Then that's even more of a reason for me to go!

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:54.800
It's enough!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.880
If you go to the Kuhouins, it won't end how it did last time.

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:00.310
I won't be able to move forward if I run away now!

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.710
There's nothing behind me!

00:18:01.710 --> 00:18:03.090
Right, that's true, but-

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:06.740
And even then, you knew I would fail, yet you let us go back to the apartment.

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:11.200
I was just happy that you didn't run away and faced it head on that time, you know.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.810
So I thought it was okay for you to fail.

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:14.180
Then let me go this time too!

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.400
You can't this time!

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.390
Why?!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:19.550
You can say that because you don't know the Kuhouins!

00:18:19.550 --> 00:18:21.220
You'll be killed if you delve into this!

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:22.630
I didn't die last time.

00:18:22.630 --> 00:18:24.490
Because you fought here!

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:27.610
Once you step foot on Kuhouin property, you'll be killed in an instant!

00:18:27.610 --> 00:18:29.650
I want to ask Murasaki once more!

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.630
She said it was okay, didn't she?

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:33.770
She was just made to say it!

00:18:33.770 --> 00:18:35.450
She...

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.240
She only said it because she wanted to save me.

00:18:37.240 --> 00:18:37.930
It could just be your imagination.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:40.240
Her eyes looked like she was in fear.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:42.460
She was pleading with her eyes, "I don't want to go back!"

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:43.390
You're mistaken.

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:47.980
I don't care if I'm mistaken, I want to ask Murasaki once more and hear the truth from her!

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:49.220
At any cost?

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.730
At any cost!

00:18:55.620 --> 00:18:57.530
What a stubborn child.

00:18:58.650 --> 00:18:59.500
I'm sorry.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.160
I don't think poorly of you.

00:19:02.590 --> 00:19:03.980
Yes.

00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:07.070
Why are all my pupils like this?

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:08.940
I'm sorry.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.170
Is that becoming a habit of yours?

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:11.590
No.

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.350
Do you know where the Kuhouins are?

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:21.820
I'll get the address from Ginko.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.840
We're not delivering mail here.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:26.420
Once you get there, it's not like you'll be able to find the Inner Sanctuary immediately.

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:27.340
I'll search for it.

00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:30.770
The Kuhouin estate is bigger than Marutomi Park.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:36.560
See? You don't know anything.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:40.510
Get your stuff together.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:41.910
I'm not moving.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.620
Murasaki liked it here.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.750
It's cold over there.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.820
You'll freeze to death before you fight.

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:52.800
I just can't hand you a map and say good luck, can I?

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:57.110
My dear pupil is saying that he'll fight the Kuhouins, after all.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:19:59.300
I'll take you there.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:04.130
Ah, hello?

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:08.310
About my car, did we have any studded snow tires for it?

00:20:13.570 --> 00:20:15.320
Are you going to Murasaki's place?

00:20:16.260 --> 00:20:17.440
You were listening?

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:20.920
Maybe I should prepare some beer to celebrate and wait for you.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.470
I'm underaged.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.120
It'll just be for the mood.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.080
Boy.

00:20:25.080 --> 00:20:26.280
Yes.

00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:37.120
This doesn't look good on you at all, boy.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:39.500
Give this to Murasaki.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:39.970
Yes.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:42.920
Here are the pictures from Shichi-Go-San.

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:45.730
It was hard to show them after all this happened.

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:48.210
Take these and show them to Murasaki.

00:20:48.210 --> 00:20:50.980
I'm sure she'll be happy.

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:55.560
Could we shake hands?

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.730
It's like a farewell, then.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.180
If I can remember the warmth of your hands,

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:04.950
I believe that I'll feel that my friends are protecting me when I fight.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.830
Rather than a handshake, this would be better!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.800
I-It just tickles!

00:21:09.800 --> 00:21:11.640
You won't forget with this!

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.000
It's okay!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:15.050
This is your chance to touch a young boy, Yamie-san!

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:18.480
He's not my type, but...!

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:33.810
I'm going now.

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:36.280
Take care.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:37.610
Come home soon.

00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:40.940
Yes.

00:21:54.510 --> 00:21:56.680
It's a scary place, isn't it?

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:59.430
It'll be fine.

00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:01.590
Yeah.

00:22:04.360 --> 00:22:05.970
You're coming too, Yayoi-san?

00:22:06.400 --> 00:22:07.520
Yeah.

00:22:08.230 --> 00:22:10.180
There's someone I need to pay back.

00:22:11.060 --> 00:22:12.230
I see.

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:28.450
What's the matter?

00:22:29.440 --> 00:22:30.460
It's nothing.

